    {"id": 11, "type": "manual",
     "desc": "Part (b): a correct response must say that a negative z means the score lies below the mean, here 1.5 standard deviations below, and must place it near the 7th percentile using the empirical rule -- about 5 percent of values lie beyond two standard deviations and about 32 percent beyond one, so a point 1.5 below the mean has roughly 6 to 7 percent of the distribution beneath it. Any percentile estimate between about 5 and 10 percent with a stated reason earns full credit.",
     "slot": "(b) what a negative z means, and the percentile",
